# Everything listed here is excluded from the "build context" - the snapshot of
# this folder that Docker uploads to its daemon before running the Dockerfile.
# Without this file, ~740 MB of data and your API keys would be sent on every
# single build.

# Secrets. Critical: image layers keep files even if a later step deletes them,
# so anything copied in once is readable by anyone who pulls the image.
.env
.env.*

# Training data - mounted at runtime instead of baked into the image.
downloads/
ml_dataset.json

# Local Python environment. Never copy this in: it holds Windows binaries that
# cannot run on the image's Linux, and the image installs its own deps anyway.
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Build outputs and trained artefacts.
*.pkl
*.keras
*.onnx

# Repo metadata the image does not need.
.git/
.gitignore
README.md

# Local MLflow state. Critically, mlruns/ and mlflow.db can contain metrics and
# artifacts from every run ever made locally - baking them into the image would
# both bloat it and publish local experiment history. CI asserts these are
# absent from the built image.
mlruns/
mlflow.db
.prefect/

# Candidates and caches: rebuilt inside the container when needed.
candidates/
.cache/
drift_report.html
drift_reports/

# Split manifest is regenerated from the dataset; a stale one in the image would
# describe a split the container cannot reproduce.
split_manifest.json

# Test and lint tooling stays on the CI runner.
tests/
pyproject.toml
requirements-dev.txt
VERIFIED.md
